  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia: Capacity Building of the Financial Reporting Center (FRC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: The FRC; Somaliland Bank; Somali Banks; Money Transfer Businesses (MTBs); Mobile Money Service Providers; and key DesignatedNon-Financial Professions and Business groups.  Indirect beneficiaries: National Anti-Money Laundering Committee (NAMLC) and Somali citizens, particularly poor and financially-excluded populations, relying on remittances and remittance service providers for financial services.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to build an effective, fit-for-purpose Financial Reporting Center (FRC) in Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen the FRC&#x2019;s capacity to safeguard Somalia&#x2019;s financial system from money laundering and terrorist financing in collaboration with key domestic partners (including regulators, law enforcement agencies, prosecutors, and other Somali authorities), regional and international partners and bodies as relevant, and the private sector by collecting, analyzing, and disseminating financial intelligence for the investigation and prosecution of financial crimes.</narrative>
  </description>
